# DOJ $225 Million Crypto Seizure — AML & Blockchain Tracing Case Study

## Executive Summary

This repository examines the U.S. Department of Justice's June 2025 civil forfeiture action involving approximately $225 million in cryptocurrency allegedly connected to pig-butchering investment fraud and associated money laundering activity.

The purpose of this analysis is to examine:

- Flow-of-funds tracing
- Wallet clustering
- Money laundering typologies
- Behavioral transaction analysis
- Exchange exposure
- Asset seizure opportunities

This case is particularly interesting because investigators reportedly followed victim funds through hundreds of thousands of transactions before identifying cryptocurrency ultimately subject to seizure.

---

# Background

According to the Department of Justice, investigators alleged that cryptocurrency investment fraud proceeds were laundered through a sophisticated network of wallets and transactions designed to obscure ownership and movement of funds.

Public reporting indicates investigators utilized:

- Blockchain analysis
- Financial intelligence
- Exchange cooperation
- Victim reporting
- Cross-border investigative coordination

to identify cryptocurrency ultimately linked to fraud proceeds.

Source:

https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/united-states-files-civil-forfeiture-complaint-against-225m-funds-involved-cryptocurrency

