# Behavioral Indicators Observed

Patterns investigators frequently examine in laundering networks include:

## Collection Activity

- Large numbers of inbound transactions
- Numerous unrelated counterparties
- Consistent fund aggregation

## Layering Activity

- Multiple intermediary wallets
- Rapid wallet-to-wallet movement
- Fund splitting
- Cross-chain transfers

## Consolidation Behavior

- Repeated movement into central wallets
- Transaction timing consistency
- Reuse of operational infrastructure

## Exchange Exposure

- Deposits into identifiable services
- Custodial wallet interaction
- Potential intervention points

