# AML Relevance

This case demonstrates how modern AML investigations increasingly overlap with blockchain investigations.

Investigators must often combine:

- Transaction monitoring
- Wallet tracing
- Behavioral analysis
- Financial intelligence
- OSINT
- Exchange cooperation

to reconstruct laundering networks.

Viewed individually, transactions may appear ordinary.

Viewed collectively over time, patterns emerge that can reveal broader operational infrastructure.

---

# Investigative Takeaways

Several observations stand out:

- Laundering networks often rely on transaction volume to create analytical noise.
- Collection wallets frequently become visible before operational leadership.
- Exchange exposure remains one of the most important investigative opportunities.
- Behavioral consistency often proves more valuable than any individual transaction.
- Asset seizure frequently occurs after investigators reconstruct the broader network rather than a single wallet.

Many AML and blockchain investigations appear to begin the same way:

Not with one massive red flag, but with transaction patterns that gradually stop looking accidental.

